{
  "$comment": "Context budget contract (context pipeline §5). Clients run their production cap parser / budget / slider-tick / calibration / estimate functions on each input and compare with expected. Integers compare exactly; rho / rhoHi compare with absolute tolerance 1e-12.",
  "schema": "oriveo.context.budget",
  "version": 1,
  "constants": {
    "tokenUnit": "1K = 1000 tokens",
    "rho0": 0.5,
    "ewmaAlpha": 0.3,
    "rhoClamp": [
      0.15,
      0.7
    ],
    "safetyFactor": 1.15,
    "minSamples": 3,
    "overflowMissFactor": 1.25,
    "messageOverheadTokens": 4,
    "minKnownWindow": 1024,
    "defaultMaxOutput": 8192,
    "budgetCapOptions": [
      "auto",
      "unlimited"
    ],
    "budgetCapDefault": "auto",
    "customCapMin": 32000,
    "customCapMax": 2147483647,
    "autoCapDefault": 256000,
    "priceLineCapMin": 64000,
    "capTickLadder": [
      32000,
      64000,
      128000,
      256000,
      384000,
      512000,
      768000,
      1000000,
      1500000,
      2000000
    ]
  },
  "rules": [
    "O = first positive of [user setting, recipe, model maxOutputTokens], else defaultMaxOutput.",
    "W is known only when W >= minKnownWindow (a fallback of 1 is unknown).",
    "total: R = min(max(O, ceil(0.10*W)), floor(0.5*W)); oWire = min(O, R). inputOnly: R = 0; oWire = O.",
    "U = W - R. budgetCap is \"auto\" | \"unlimited\" | custom integer c (see capCases). auto: B = min(U, autoCapDefault, T') where T' = priceLineTokens only when priceLineTokens >= priceLineCapMin (lower lines are shown in the panel / confirm dialog but never cap). unlimited: B = U. custom: B = min(max(c, customCapMin), U). priceLineTokens never affects unlimited or custom; a non-integer priceLineTokens is treated as absent. A custom value is clamped into [customCapMin, customCapMax] before min with U, so no constructed value can bypass the parse range. Clients without a known price line pass no priceLineTokens.",
    "limitedBy names the bound that set B: custom | priceLine | autoDefault | window. Ties prefer the user-facing bound: custom over window; priceLine over autoDefault over window. null when B is null.",
    "derived: preCompactAt = floor(0.75B), sendCompactAt = floor(0.90B), compactTargetMax = floor(0.50B), reminderAt = floor(0.30B), tail = clamp(floor(0.25B), 4000, 48000), userMessagesMax = min(16000, floor(0.10B)), summaryMax = min(4000, max(1000, floor(0.05B))), systemMax = min(floor(0.25B), 32000), recallMax = floor(0.07B).",
    "Unknown W: R and U are null, oWire = O. auto / unlimited: B and derived are null, proactive compaction is off (reactive only, §8.6). custom c: B = max(c, customCapMin), derived from B, proactive compaction on (desktop A6 §3.2.5).",
    "est text = ceil(utf8Bytes * rhoHi); est message = est text + messageOverheadTokens.",
    "Calibration sample = (observedInput - mediaTokens) / textBytes; skipped when observedInput is null, textBytes <= 0 or the ratio <= 0. observedInput = input_uncached + cache_read + cache_write_5m + cache_write_1h.",
    "Samples 1-2 are collected only; the 3rd sets rho = clamp(mean(samples 1..3)); later samples: rho = clamp(alpha*sample + (1-alpha)*rho). Evaluate exactly in that operand order (IEEE double).",
    "rhoHi = rho * safetyFactor once n >= minSamples, else rho (rho0 unless an overflow miss raised it).",
    "Overflow miss (predicted pHat < U but the provider reported overflow): rho = min(0.70, rho * 1.25).",
    "pHat with a previous observed input and no compaction since: observedPrevious - estDynamicPrevious + estAnswerPrevious + sum(estNewMessages) + estDynamicNow; otherwise the full estimate.",
    "Ring display: percent = ceil(100 * pHat / B); tone warm at >= 70, error after an overflow; window unknown -> unavailable; never observed (estimated only) -> unavailable with estimatedPercent shown in the panel only. Never show 0% for an unmeasured value.",
    "Cap parsing (capCases): exactly \"auto\" and \"unlimited\" are accepted as strings; an integral-valued number in [customCapMin, customCapMax] is custom (64000.0 counts as 64000, since JavaScript and some decoders cannot tell them apart); everything else (smaller / larger / fractional numbers, legacy \"64k\"-style keys, numeric strings, other case, empty, null, booleans) is rejected and the caller treats the stored value as absent. customCapMax = 2^31 - 1 keeps Kotlin Int and Swift Int identical.",
    "Slider ticks (capTickCases): sorted unique (capTickLadder ∪ {priceLineTokens when >= customCapMin}) ∩ [customCapMin, U], plus U itself; U unknown -> no upper bound and U is not added; U < customCapMin -> [U]. The slider binds to the tick index; typed values commit through the custom rule above."
  ],
